Forager patch 0006: orchards, plant nurseries and vineyards in the landuse layer, each told apart by kind_detail
(dispatch 2026-10-31-coder-06; the owner: "Orchards, Plant nurseries, Vineyards").

Against protomaps/basemaps at ca93fc06efbaff1c5f069d06edbe5de18839c1c8 (tiles 4.15.2), with 0001 to 0005 already
applied. Applied after them with `git apply` by map-build/bin/build-basemap-jar.sh.

Upstream writes landuse=orchard (and farmyard) as kind farmland, and writes nothing for plant_nursery or vineyard.
With this patch all three are kind farmland, and carry kind_detail = orchard, plant_nursery or vineyard, so a style
that draws farmland draws them as before and a style can tell each apart. kind_detail is set only where the kind
stayed farmland: an orchard whose kind a later rule takes over (a national park) gets none. Farmyards and farmland
are unchanged, with no kind_detail.

Landuse.postProcess merges neighbouring polygons with the same attributes only at zooms 6 and below, so there an
orchard, nursery or vineyard no longer merges with plain farmland beside it. At 7 to 15 nothing is merged, before or
after.

Pinned by 6 forager* cases in LanduseTest (foragerOrchardKindDetail 3, foragerNoKindDetail 3).

